  {
    "type": "post",
    "title": "Can a vertiport actually make money? I started from the bottom up — not with projected passenger demand, but with the smallest functional facility I could model: 1 TLOF, 2 stands, ",
    "company": "",
    "location": "",
    "text": "Can a vertiport actually make money? I started from the bottom up — not with projected passenger demand, but with the smallest functional facility I could model: 1 TLOF, 2 stands, charging, ARFF and a 1,000 sqm terminal. The result surprised me. At full capacity, the facility generates about ₹3.4 crore in annual revenue, yet the project IRR is only around 2% — before land and taxes. The problem is not simply CAPEX. It is how much revenue a vertiport can extract from each four-seat aircraft movement without damaging the operator's economics. This is Part 1. The next question is whether a network of vertiports changes the economics. #Vertiports #AdvancedAirMobility #AirportPlanning #Aviation #InfrastructureFinance https://lnkd.in/dh8sNJnF",
    "url": "",
